                <pb facs="0307" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/381: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-18T00:00:00-05:45">January 18,
                        1934—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received January 19—3:16 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Department’s telegram No. 8, January 18, 2 p.m. In accordance with
                    instructions have telegraphed [draft protocol?] to Legation at Tegucigalpa in my
                    January 18, midnight.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
